    IDS_STRING1028          "Delete"
    IDS_STRING1029          "Cancel"
    IDS_STRING1030          "\010-Producers-\010\nJay Minn\nTravis Baldree"
    IDS_STRING1031          "\010-Design/Programming-\010\nTravis Baldree"
    IDS_STRING1032          "\010-Art Direction-\010\nTravis Baldree"
    IDS_STRING1033          "\010-Artists-\010\nJason Beck, Kevin Green, Jeff Selbig, Mike Fisher\nDavid Johnson, Travis Baldree, Martin Bartsch, Tito Pagan\nLiquid Development, Donnavon Webb, Nikitova, Jurgen Brenkert, David Helsby"
    IDS_STRING1034          "\010-Test Lead-\010\nMarcus King"
    IDS_STRING1035          "\010-Testers-\010\nScott Branston, Greg Brown, Tony Case\nBill Dennes, John Dunbar, Todd Dyment\nDeon Miyoi, Chris Mosconi, Sergio Sanchez"
    IDS_STRING1036          "\010-Audio-\010\nMarc Pospisil, Travis Baldree\nAdditional Music Licensed from LicenseMusic.com\nVoice Talents of Henry Dardennes, Lynn McManus, Dave White, John Patrick Lowrie"
    IDS_STRING1037          "Since oldest living memory, the \010Dungeon Gate\010 has been standing in the heart of the \010Old Wood\010.  Its doorway leads to infinite possibility, to \010subterranean lands\010 fabled in stories and myths.  Many \010adventurers\010 have passed over that ancient threshold - some to find \010fame\010, \010glory\010, and \010wealth\010 beyond telling, and others \010never to return\010.\n\nThe town of \010Grove\010 has forever been the safe haven at the Dungeon's mouth - a watering hole and resting place for weary adventurers.  Here great tales are told by the Inn's fire.  \010Journeys\010 are planned, and \010legacies\010 are made.  \010Minstrels\010 sing of the great feats of \010heroes\010 long gone, and \010statues\010 ring the square, a testament to their deeds.\n\nAfter travelling many hard and dusty days, you and your faithful \010companion\010 arrive at last in the fabled forest town, which awaits beneath the long shadow of the \010Gate\010.\n\nWithin these walls lies the path to \010infinite adventure\010. It is here that you will test your worth, and perhaps find \010fortune\010 and \010glory\010 along the way. It is here that you will determine your \010Fate...\010"
    IDS_STRING1038          "Continue..."
    IDS_STRING1039          "Since oldest living memory, the \010Dungeon Gate\010 has been standing in the heart of the \010Old Wood\010.  Its doorway leads to infinite possibility, to \010subterranean lands\010 fabled in stories and myths.  Many \010adventurers\010 have passed over that ancient threshold - some to find \010fame\010, \010glory\010, and \010wealth\010 beyond telling, and others \010never to return\010.\n\nThe town of \010Grove\010 has forever been the safe haven at the Dungeon's mouth - a watering hole and resting place for weary adventurers.  Here great tales are told by the Inn's fire.  \010Journeys\010 are planned, and \010legacies\010 are made.  \010Minstrels\010 sing of the great feats of \010heroes\010 long gone, and \010statues\010 ring the square, a testament to their deeds.\n\nAfter travelling many hard and dusty days, you and your faithful \010companion\010 arrive at last in the fabled forest town, which awaits beneath the long shadow of the \010Gate\010.\n\nWithin these walls lies the path to \010infinite adventure\010. It is here that you will test your worth, and perhaps find \010fortune\010 and \010glory\010 along the way. It is here that you will determine your \010Fate...\010"
END

